Notebook[{
Cell["Watching a Quantum Particle", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"a294e293-6048-4317-bbcd-34d31e164b74"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Simulating the stochastic Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger \
equation of continuous position measurement with the Wolfram Language: where \
the equation comes from, what it tells you before you ever run it, how to \
integrate it correctly, and how to know that you did.",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bf44de04-d9eb-4a3f-a484-\
16d81b02de7f"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: July 22, 2026)", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f4d16a20-36c6-4786-98da-ee06904f3225"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: How This Document Flows", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ece07c86-9163-46dd-b8e6-9e0618176d8d"],

Cell["\<\
This is a computational essay on the continuous quantum measurement: how a \
weak Gaussian detector turns into a stochastic differential equation, why \
that equation is nonlinear but not violating no-signaling, what its \
conditional variances do before you simulate anything, and how to properly \
compute dynamical equations and relevant observables in Wolfram Mathematica.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0ae0f045-d79b-467d-9733-4dfbf64363cc"],

Cell["\<\
This essay is meant to be understand computationally. It means the code \
should do the heavy lifting for grasping some complicated concepts. Although \
some codes may look complicated, but focus on the output and its meaning \
before worrying about every detail of the input. And remember that you are \
not locked into the code as given. You can (and should) modify it, and run \
your own numerical experiments.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"06e3404a-7899-4c6e-bd2e-244425a9b010"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "I assume the reader is familiar with quantum theory at nonrelativistic \
Schrodinger equation, and enough Wolfram Language to read codes. No \
stochastic calculus is assumed: the two It\[OHat] facts we need are \
introduced where they are used. The pace steepens where we hand the kernel \
the canonical commutation relation and let it do the operator algebra. \
Throughout, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f2e93796-ec2c-4571-ba9d-446c8c145207"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a6cc376-6066-4192-9816-864d2000acb8"],
 " and the measurement strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c6c308b8-99f8-431f-b78a-940e877c6df8"],
 " stay symbolic for as long as possible."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"751443e7-2062-4e8c-bb37-79bd92673f1b"],

Cell["Let's start.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cbe91cfc-9fe4-4ca6-95fb-92a2ae3fe2a9"],

Cell["Part I: From a Detector to a Differential Equation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"20ac649f-19db-4543-93ac-c3eb271373da"],

Cell["The It\[OHat] Equation: The Continuum Limit of Weak Measurement", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"09cb19b0-4182-4863-8c0d-7b1edf8e8b91"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "96d786e2-9aec-47d2-bd03-57dc842ac567"],
 " and write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c672e60-1e9d-4ea5-bf59-dc2ec11caab7"],
 ". During the interval ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79a01d35-02bf-4cad-8b41-491bb6fbb6fd"],
 ", which we will call bin ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c962e1dc-4499-4eb5-8f83-1a0bcbb5859e"],
 ", the detector directly returns one real number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3aca968c-2b01-435d-90e4-69281a05ddf3"],
 ". The sequence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4097430b-71ab-4f68-9ec6-459bf350b645"],
 " is the measurement record at finite time resolution."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"675bf057-a8b0-4b43-a22e-b25c2395ac4c"],

Cell["\<\
The measurement during one interval is defined by the Gaussian measurement \
operators\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e55b0dc8-022a-439d-b40c-107625a0f5fb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"2", 
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "\[Pi]"], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"3cab31e5-56c1-4850-\
a590-26f87210647e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8daab481-6acf-488b-978e-a64bdb9af6af"],
 " is the measurement strength. The prefactor ensures"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d2f82aa-1253-4920-9309-1dcb701d08bd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", 
     RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}], "\[Infinity]",
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"932d25bb-4f17-4f46-\
99c1-f0b31c29045f"],

Cell["\<\
Consequently, the same measurement operator determines both the probability \
density of the detector output,\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"70c21dc1-d46d-4182-b893-1bc557fce709"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {GridBox[{
          {
           RowBox[{
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
            RowBox[{
             StyleBox["(",
              SpanMaxSize->1], 
             SubscriptBox[
              OverscriptBox[
               StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
              StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
             StyleBox[")",
              SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
            TemplateBox[{
              SubscriptBox[
               StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
               StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
             "Ket"]}]}
         },
         GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
         GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}], "2"]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"7c3e3634-64a5-4e5e-\
bb36-55b62b371f7f"],

Cell["and the state conditioned on the measured value,", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ae54e212-78c4-4d48-9515-98503144dc64"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["k", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]},
     "Ket"], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["U", "TI"], "^"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      TemplateBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
       "Ket"]}], GridBox[{
       {GridBox[{
          {
           RowBox[{
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["U", "TI"], "^"], 
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
            RowBox[{
             StyleBox["(",
              SpanMaxSize->1], 
             SubscriptBox[
              OverscriptBox[
               StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
              StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
             StyleBox[")",
              SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
            TemplateBox[{
              SubscriptBox[
               StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
               StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
             "Ket"]}]}
         },
         GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
         GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["U", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"56872e42-fb4e-440e-\
b5e2-6105de62ceb9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To make the output density explicit, write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
    "BraKet"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a22e7d8c-d836-4a8b-ba3b-cf064826c705"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["x", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["x", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04d58f3a-d80c-4f3b-95cd-0ceb6ff4c28d"],
 ". Then"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0b81f651-d5c2-444b-9899-1fbc6dad5824"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    SqrtBox[
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "\[Pi]"]], 
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Integral]", 
     RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}], "\[Infinity]",
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", "2", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
         StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"61c1c348-63ca-46a4-\
be42-135d8891fda5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Gaussian kernel is normalized and centered at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3df1940e-3da6-4609-9cd5-02742786041a"],
 ", with variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b39f5000-651f-4226-a569-7b69510a0395"],
 ". The detector-output density is therefore the Born position density \
blurred by the detector response, which is also a recipe for sampling one \
reading: draw ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7eb2c077-e001-4d23-bdb1-36e2dda4b9f9"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c4a7f4b-2d22-40d4-bb70-1b5405c8702b"],
 ", then add independent detector noise of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fc759db3-6b51-479d-8ef3-245aed04dfda"],
 ". Because the kernel is centered, the conditional mean and variance follow \
at once:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1052bced-883b-48bc-b0b3-a2d8d94d54d1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\|01d53c", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["Var",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1,
        FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         RowBox[{
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
          SubscriptBox[
           RowBox[{
            StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
             SpanMaxSize->1], 
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
            StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
             SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
           StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1,
        FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "+", 
     FractionBox["1", 
      RowBox[{"4", 
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"339a681d-82f2-4c6a-\
bfa5-89b0dab8b97c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[Congruent]", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
     "Bra"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3cc63b50-5d2f-4956-9c45-5f23e691230d"],
 " is evaluated before the reading in bin ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bf8bf9b5-e43c-472e-b6f2-6c8c360a3557"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eeddbb2d-3f79-4adf-91e7-eff14bfe801c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The raw readings have no continuous-time limit, since that variance \
diverges as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "28881277-2c2e-4510-a727-425009820a55"],
 ". What does have one is the accumulated record, and the way it accumulates \
fixes both the power of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9b713b40-8f85-4ee2-bc1f-306035dc8f8c"],
 " and the constant in front. Scale the readings as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20c67e1f-f9d6-4b94-8def-f99c97fbf926"],
 " and add up the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e0d4136a-a342-4be5-95a4-20a70a4b54aa"],
 " bins in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d8b46d7-2dba-4eeb-ab6a-e94324254ee8"],
 "; the detector noise is independent from bin to bin, so the variances add, \
giving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", "4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "-", "2"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bd2d33c3-bee1-41d0-8b9c-ea1a889dce4b"],
 " to leading order. This is finite and nonzero only at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a450d11a-9b71-4a5d-a906-7c0d789542d0"],
 "; at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a947c3df-810e-4afe-8e28-21d0c6bed5bc"],
 " the accumulated noise diverges, and at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", "3", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e201c20a-1eea-4f5d-8782-cd84f0879e0e"],
 " it vanishes, leaving a deterministic record. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2db5405-f7f9-47b7-9c3a-72fbacef5385"],
 " fixed, the choice ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03568c42-c5cd-4707-af86-5c7df1b2e87d"],
 " makes the accumulated variance exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34b1f0e9-e054-493b-b054-d9d94d003e4f"],
 ", which is the statement ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4eea2ef6-fb63-4819-9784-bff176f29571"],
 ". Neither choice is free. Define"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5c0de3dc-70a0-4d82-9d2f-37efaafd1dfe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "0"], "=", "0"}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], "\[Congruent]", 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "+", 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "."}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"fdbd1121-4d8a-485b-\
a821-3b0e5c1a7c0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The detector still measures ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e03acab4-2f79-4c36-b722-c1799f27b2c1"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d6d6a78c-ad13-4d09-b604-f22b30677dc3"],
 " is computed from those readings; it is a repackaging, not an additional \
measured quantity, since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "91dc3757-6119-4299-ad2e-abe231e72d82"],
 " recovers them exactly."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"38b0b367-e448-4fb9-806f-f3685b4c5961"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The mean above gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d53c", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d43344f8-e35b-45f6-b877-3effeddb72b5"],
 ". Remove it from the record increment:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"77ca6f10-9a8e-4d91-a287-e1d0ac8db4a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[Congruent]", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", "2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"96aae2c0-f06c-4d34-\
b158-57b43fc9d72c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nothing new is being assumed about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e752ffc9-371e-442e-9ddf-c9429190373e"],
 ": this relation is exact and invertible, so its law is inherited from the \
measured-output law rather than imposed alongside it. Because the relation is \
affine, it carries the two-step sampling recipe through term by term:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e7ae367e-0c93-42c1-a10c-c1f192a0c8ca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", 
    UnderscriptBox[
     UnderscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"2", 
       SqrtBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
       SubscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
         StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox[")",
        FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], "\[UnderBrace]"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"Born", "\[NonBreakingSpace]", "draw"}],
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox[
     UnderscriptBox[
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[UnderBrace]"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"detector", "\[NonBreakingSpace]", "noise"}],
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[Tilde]", 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[Tilde]", 
    RowBox[{"\|01d4a9", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1054ed5e-5312-4a9e-\
b45f-5ca7d22588c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The rescaled detector noise is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d4a9", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10fa7043-af8c-4bb2-86ff-11847773961c"],
 " at every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75b42c35-6773-4f13-8bb9-01262fe9e0b2"],
 ", which is what the constant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5189b115-d9e3-463b-a11e-0378b91d20c0"],
 " was chosen to arrange. The Born draw has mean zero, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d53c", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e2f7e664-945a-48df-bcf3-5f6f8d88f9ea"],
 " exactly, and it is the only state-dependent piece. Its variance relative \
to the detector's is"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ffb0f336-e64d-41b0-9298-00ed899e7a16"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"4", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], 
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1,
       FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
           StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1,
        FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "=", "4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1,
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
       SubscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
         StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1,
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[LongRightArrow]", "0"}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1c060470-65ad-424a-\
8784-dc599c2408cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So provided the position variance stays finite, the state washes out of the \
noise and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb5dd73b-a861-4cb4-a331-221a93f9816d"],
 " becomes Gaussian with mean zero and variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c5bc3d0f-efad-4336-865e-7a204415f1cc"],
 ". Since that limiting law no longer refers to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cd351211-bbd2-4d11-bf51-c4c87833dc3c"],
 ", it does not refer to the earlier readings that determined ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "efcbd7de-99e5-4bfb-a8c5-79344597b403"],
 " either; repeating the same detector rule in every bin therefore gives \
independent increments, whose cumulative sum converges to a Wiener process ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a393e37b-7153-40ed-b475-dc51b08d61ec"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5fff6ed5-ae54-42f7-b73d-23f26f85643e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We now derive the finite-bin state update. Every coefficient is evaluated \
from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0bf94b7e-badb-49c9-b809-51cb312a6ee9"],
 " before ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b55f530-e471-4552-9412-68fce3c1bc5f"],
 " is measured; this beginning-of-bin convention will give the It\[OHat] \
equation in the continuum limit. From the definition of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dd745a0b-9199-40c6-bc2a-6b54db7b7614"],
 ","
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2ea14e24-ce71-4638-86ba-8d2ce0e3df21"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      SqrtBox[
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8a97d422-d00a-4b0f-\
b107-a1fcc65b220b"],

Cell["Define", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"827d32c4-179a-44b5-b21d-168b14328bf2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[Congruent]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"bc13d23a-b87d-4082-\
9b38-52ede860b7c5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Substitution into the exponent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d18559cc-2d67-40c2-9b25-d3f177c31ad5"],
 " gives"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f9cf6425-0c19-4599-b504-b3b8b9ceae47"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[GridBox[{
    {
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{"=", 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox[
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
           StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
          FractionBox[
           RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
            SubscriptBox[
             StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
             StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
           RowBox[{"2", 
            SqrtBox[
             StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
            StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}], ")"}], "2"]}]}]},
    {"", 
     RowBox[{"=", 
      RowBox[{
       SqrtBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "-", 
       FractionBox[
        SuperscriptBox[
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["(",
           SpanMaxSize->1], 
          RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
          StyleBox[")",
           SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
        RowBox[{"4", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}], "."}]}
   },
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {Right, {Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"67a44e94-82b0-4de0-\
9f4d-23a06046fb65"],

Cell["\<\
The last term is a scalar: it multiplies the entire state by the same \
positive number and cancels exactly in the normalized update. Only\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8fab515a-e558-44c6-a35f-b24bf6563cca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"fc35423e-5638-408e-\
a50f-3a73fea4e331"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "can change the normalized state. Since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a8261d99-9509-477d-a32b-083eeb12b01d"],
 ", its finite-bin expansion is"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25211c7c-8ea2-4186-af5d-c96165d2ddc8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      SqrtBox[
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "=", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "2"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "+", 
    StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}]]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"d1d8a4fb-6166-402f-\
9e4b-8cb8faa1925e"],

Cell["The finite-bin unitary factor is", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0778e22f-123d-48aa-b2ff-04de84a70b69"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["U", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f33edbaa-f213-4d76-\
b17c-a489423ea021"],

Cell["\<\
All finite-bin quantities have now been expanded. Take the continuum limit \
once:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6b150205-b88e-46e0-aa3f-db48b37727c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[LongRightArrow]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[LongRightArrow]", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]}], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "\[LongRightArrow]", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]}], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b51b2aa9-559c-4b77-\
82bd-f394403dffa5"],

Cell["The measurement factor becomes", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c6ff9974-6c9b-438d-84e6-e2c8f4a95624"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "\[Congruent]", 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"ab72d288-de75-4740-\
8a37-c80c3b702233"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its squared norm differs from one by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "-", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c8731b1-3a7b-4043-a128-1925eeeefe39"],
 ", so normalization adds no term. The record equation is therefore"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d664e053-1a90-486b-ad7e-e74bd2ee7118"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"c553a657-b373-4733-\
aaef-759b1f2ca3e9"],

Cell["\<\
Multiplying the measurement and unitary factors gives the state equation\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"576ea07f-7b4d-412d-bf05-a0483b62b53d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        FractionBox[
         StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"]}], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
         RowBox[{
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
          SubscriptBox[
           RowBox[{
            StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
             SpanMaxSize->1], 
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
            StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
             SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
           StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], "2"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       SqrtBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
           StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]}], "]"}], 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]]},
      "Ket"], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8b454c49-aa89-4bb4-\
96f7-cc24bbff756a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39d53dc5-bbff-4a6d-aa39-971e37118630"],
 " appears here and in the record equation because it is the centered random \
part of the measured record."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6894d5ea-b517-4073-a308-af412a9426ca"],

Cell["The Norm Cancellation Along a Conditioned Trajectory", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"89009228-0e0a-400c-9d42-6fb479f83f87"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let us verify the norm claim rather than assert it. Suppress the time \
subscript and write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aae2d00-4e06-4a1c-b394-1a2e296f7382"],
 ". For an It\[OHat] equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["D", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["N", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0351fbdb-beb4-41b6-a1c9-4e1b4c6e3919"],
 ", the product rule gives"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9e36039b-37b0-4312-ae94-a214531816b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "BraKet"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["N", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["N", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["W", "TI"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["D", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["D", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["N", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["N", "TI"], "^"]}]}], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"29f5161d-9934-4f13-\
8ced-3fb1e62851c7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the equation above, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], "^"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "/", "\[HBar]", "-", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dc79e81-f4df-4f03-874d-9fe4ae1961eb"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["N", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9ba07285-be77-4a5f-bb5a-f4548dae1751"],
 ". The noise coefficient vanishes because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11529b9a-79ce-4080-878c-76b9bd533c00"],
 ". The remaining drift contains ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["D", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "af7cfcd6-1597-4972-af29-8ce826eb5983"],
 " and the It\[OHat] correction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["N", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["N", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a9e6befc-fdb5-4276-8354-c9e61b5e33c1"],
 ". The constants ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b728cc2-3e88-4940-a70c-b39e7fcd9d9d"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77a14672-707b-4160-92f7-40846822c387"],
 " do not affect this cancellation, so set them to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e006d096-fb7f-4437-b10c-8379beef722d"],
 " and define a function that tests the drift for a random Hamiltonian, a \
random measured observable and a random state in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d34318fa-6c79-4bfe-a491-4fb3a300c957"],
 " dimensions:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5881333b-6abc-4da5-8e9b-9614bcd40702"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "normDrift", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"normDrift", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"h", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", " ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], "@", 
         RowBox[{"RandomComplex", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "1"}], " ", "-", " ", "I"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", "I"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{"xop", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", " ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], "@", 
         RowBox[{"RandomComplex", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "1"}], " ", "-", " ", "I"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", "I"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Psi]", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
         RowBox[{"RandomComplex", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "1"}], " ", "-", " ", "I"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", "I"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "n"}], 
          "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"xop", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "xop", 
           " ", ".", " ", "\[Psi]"}], ")"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "n", "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dOp", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "h"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"a", " ", ".", " ", "a"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"dOp", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "dOp", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "a", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         "a"}]}], ")"}], " ", ".", " ", "\[Psi]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"24ab2ffc-1675-4e73-8e01-74520fd8d352"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The multi-argument ",
 Cell[BoxData["With"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a41b367-b8c3-4a1c-8bcc-fb8cec50f276"],
 " (successive binding lists ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"h", ",", "..."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "a", "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "dOp", "}"}], ",", " ", "body"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "97144e06-2657-4aa0-a821-76e4e0b4b0ab"],
 ", each list seeing the ones before it) keeps every intermediate a named \
constant rather than a reassigned variable, without a tower of nested \
brackets. Now run it across dimensions and read the result:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"17db8004-1d64-4726-bdde-6704b0acf0a6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"normDrift", "[", "n", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"86a59ac1-9290-4389-9b7f-6c0d1781102d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here ",
 Cell[BoxData["Chop"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "710a1028-645e-4a68-9225-8053111469c5"],
 " sets tiny machine-precision residue to zero so the output reads cleanly. \
As one can see, the norm drift vanishes in every tested dimension for \
independently generated Hermitian operators and states. Together with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "115b0784-0ee6-418b-8fa5-fb60e2c255be"],
 ", this confirms norm preservation through It\[OHat] order. Note that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b1b95d1f-f758-4ae7-bb0e-85fedf84e005"],
 " drops out entirely, so the cancellation is a property of the measurement \
terms."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ae30d711-fe13-4e95-a27e-55deadd66640"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This cancellation keeps every fully conditioned trajectory normalized and \
pure. It does not imply that the measurement causes no decoherence. If the \
detector record is ignored and the projectors ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]]},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]]},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a7afa03f-c146-4a09-a6db-e250cb773d1d"],
 " are averaged over all possible records, the resulting density operator \
contains the measurement dissipator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37518849-f6a4-4419-9b87-ce3fcd18c5ff"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07538f1b-059a-40f4-ab49-82c1082706fb"],

Cell["Part II: What the Equation Says Before You Simulate It", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b8a01373-6327-4bba-80d7-3adf79634528"],

Cell["The Canonical Commutator: One Relation, Handed to the Kernel", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e6b7aea1-b6db-45b7-af9d-63a59afe5faa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here is a habit worth acquiring: before writing a simulation, extract every \
exact statement you can, because those become the benchmarks that catch the \
simulation being wrong. For this equation a great deal is exactly computable, \
and all of it follows from one commutator, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e221ee0-3013-4345-874f-2249582bce56"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6624e3e0-9aac-419f-9ab4-df86c5c93f99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Version 15.0 added a noncommutative-algebra system to the Wolfram Language, \
so we no longer hand-roll an operator ordering. We declare the two generators \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c8670476-5593-462d-bacd-347235933818"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f9c93a97-1816-49f2-a83a-192e78999fb0"],
 " and the single relation between them, and let ",
 Cell[BoxData["NonCommutativeAlgebra"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fb12cd51-dcee-45eb-982f-d5ac2c7d82fc"],
 " carry the algebra. The commutation relation is entered \
leading-monomial-positive, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]", "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "618fb03f-ba43-40ce-8236-d101993ae739"],
 ", which says ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62512d01-e9cc-4bb4-8d5e-85df0fe5263e"],
 ". Define the algebra and two thin wrappers for expanding and for \
commutators:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bd1fda71-d16b-478d-ad10-bb7f12c0cab7"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"xp", ",", " ", "nc", ",", " ", "comm"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xp", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"NonCommutativeAlgebra", "[", 
    RowBox[{"<|", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<Generators\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"xo", ",", " ", "po"}], "}"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<CommutationRelations\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"po", " ", "**", " ", "xo"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"xo", " ", "**", " ", "po"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[HBar]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "|>"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"nc", "[", "e_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"NonCommutativeExpand", "[", 
    RowBox[{"e", ",", " ", "xp"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
    RowBox[{"a_", ",", " ", "b_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"nc", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Commutator", "[", 
     RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b", ",", " ", "xp"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"xp", "[", "\"\<Unity\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"39ef0451-042e-4df5-a706-132aa7b94adc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The algebra's unity is a plain ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b7d3ef1b-75de-4c7f-946a-dbca24dd5d32"],
 ", not a stray formal object, which matters more than it looks: a \
hand-rolled ",
 Cell[BoxData["NonCommutativeMultiply"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ae71f36-84f7-47db-8b6d-a55f52706160"],
 " has no identity reduction and leaks empty products into everything \
downstream, and here that whole class of bug simply does not exist. Now check \
the one relation, the double commutator we will need for the heating law, and \
a normal-ordering:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"31728703-f065-4d66-963e-da85c55af1cb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
    RowBox[{"xo", ",", " ", "po"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
    RowBox[{"xo", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
      RowBox[{"xo", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"po", " ", "**", " ", "po"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"nc", "[", 
    RowBox[{"xo", " ", "**", " ", "po", " ", "**", " ", "xo"}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"19db6693-9450-4111-831c-38e6b6ad0865"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the canonical commutator is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b492a487-37ba-4949-93e4-3a4852746679"],
 ", the double commutator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "-", "2", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68d764e1-235d-4f11-be4a-a840c7231109"],
 " is a c-number, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["NonCommutativeExpand"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0dc3bffe-c78c-49c0-9c45-7fd655dedae8"],
 " puts every product into canonical form with all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "479b7473-68dc-4b79-826a-8d96f2d7b5ef"],
 " to the left of all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dad45b2e-c85e-458e-8147-ecdda4c0397c"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e222ac9d-2e63-4931-a066-a879205db3b1"],
 " normal-orders to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b59e843d-15b9-49cb-ad25-039c8c8e5a1a"],
 ". That canonical form is exactly the normal ordering we need for the \
Gaussian closure below."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04776f13-b4c2-4fca-bf6d-e679be489a92"],

Cell["The Heating Law: One Line, and It Is Exact", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"500cfa1e-2c86-430d-9428-30f3c4ce1397"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Averaging the stochastic equation over the noise gives back a Lindblad \
equation, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "."], "=", "-", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b8406009-bb7f-4fc4-b7ec-b6d48b4e7d75"],
 ". That means the ensemble-averaged rate of change of any observable ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8485b745-44ba-4c45-9cb0-ca659e6aa1fa"],
 " picks up a term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["O", "TI"], "^"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "167659a5-24a4-4951-a358-b06699f33d3e"],
 ". For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["O", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42142cf1-ecd2-40da-b6de-f342cafaed5a"],
 " we already have the double commutator in hand:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fde3a4ef-c948-4818-8eb1-139e75317966"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nc", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
   RowBox[{"Commutator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"xo", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Commutator", "[", 
      RowBox[{"xo", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"po", " ", "**", " ", "po"}], ",", " ", "xp"}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", "xp"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e5ffd39e-080b-4407-9a81-0d789e6e4d06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Therefore ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "\|01d53c", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "be3fe609-f07e-45eb-b1c6-e86a4d8fbca8"],
 ", exactly, with no approximation. Look at what this does ",
 StyleBox["not", "TI"],
 " depend on: not the state, not the mass, not the Hamiltonian (as long as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "389908fd-3b30-4528-8b69-8409de3e182b"],
 " conserves ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d9ac0b7-864c-4aa8-9a7f-fb0c6af94d4a"],
 " on its own, as a free particle does). Watching a particle's position heats \
it at a fixed rate forever, which is the price the uncertainty principle \
charges for position information. This will be our sharpest numerical \
benchmark, precisely because it is a straight line with a known slope and \
nothing to tune."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5164fd22-6460-4ca5-9b04-4f48e580efb3"],

Cell["Gaussian Closure: Wick's Theorem for Noncommuting Moments", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"af069402-0bd0-4c4c-934e-7f11d5309eb3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To get the conditional variances we need expectation values of \
normal-ordered monomials in a Gaussian state. For Gaussian states all moments \
follow from the first two by Wick's theorem, pairing factors two at a time. \
The one subtlety is that the pairing is ",
 StyleBox["order-dependent", "TI"],
 " here, because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ab16be4-7ecc-48f3-bc91-94741af7bc8b"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e7c29edd-0ed3-44a5-9425-1c91de0147ec"],
 " do not commute: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3529cf93-1ef5-46d5-9f49-03b06b87872c"],
 " while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13613f6f-1a00-4b95-b7ad-b60cef1e7f6a"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ab18913b-faea-4693-b4eb-05fe642034d1"],
 " is the symmetrized covariance."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8311b350-71db-4825-959e-37cc1a06f46f"],

Cell["\<\
Set the two-point data (the covariances, ordered) and the pairing recursion \
that builds every higher even moment from them:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f35dc7dc-5ecf-48cb-8606-6492c47839dc"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"cov", ",", " ", "wick"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"cov", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<x\>\""}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   "Vx"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"cov", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<p\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<p\>\""}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   "Vp"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"cov", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<p\>\""}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Cc", " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"I", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "2"}]}]}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"cov", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<p\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<x\>\""}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Cc", " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"I", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "2"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"wick", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", "}"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", "1"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"wick", "[", 
    RowBox[{"l_", " ", "/;", " ", 
     RowBox[{"OddQ", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Length", "@", "l"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", "0"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"wick", "[", "l_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"cov", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"First", "@", "l"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"l", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "k", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"wick", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Delete", "[", 
        RowBox[{"l", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", "k", "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Length", "@", "l"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4bf1d561-c30d-4d6e-af16-9899d1a69d5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, ",
 Cell[BoxData["wick"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ca9dd49-79a1-446a-a547-e976a69081b6"],
 " pairs the first fluctuation with each later one, multiplies by that pair's \
covariance, and recurses on what is left. Now the map from a canonical \
operator monomial to its Gaussian expectation. The canonical form from ",
 Cell[BoxData["NonCommutativeExpand"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "96208123-574e-4f32-8071-8c328ab0c8be"],
 " writes repeated factors as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"GeneralizedPower", "[", 
   RowBox[{"NonCommutativeMultiply", ",", " ", "g", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3389aa4b-cf7b-4b0d-99a4-51af397915c9"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData["letters"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c9183a3e-b5a3-45d8-aa42-f9fcc38ed78a"],
 " flattens a monomial into its list of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c176116-79ea-40a2-b3b4-f02d1e77f406"],
 "'s and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f49a7084-97c4-4407-9a57-a03ce886ac52"],
 "'s, ",
 Cell[BoxData["monExp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "988abfd1-662b-488f-abe9-8d229be8cf15"],
 " splits every letter into mean plus fluctuation and Wick-contracts the \
fluctuations, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["gExp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f77d931d-beef-4712-aa84-b23581028f81"],
 " applies that to a whole expanded polynomial:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"18664962-6b3d-4e22-b14b-4e60d6a46068"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"letters", ",", " ", "monExp", ",", " ", "gExp"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"letters", "[", 
    RowBox[{"HoldPattern", "[", 
     RowBox[{"NonCommutativeMultiply", "[", "a__", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"Join", " ", "@@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"letters", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "a", "}"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"letters", "[", 
    RowBox[{"GeneralizedPower", "[", 
     RowBox[{"NonCommutativeMultiply", ",", " ", "g_", ",", " ", "k_"}], 
     "]"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"letters", "[", "xo", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "xo", "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"letters", "[", "po", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "po", "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"monExp", "[", "ls_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"If", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"#2", " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"#1", " ", "/.", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"xo", " ", "->", " ", "mx"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"po", " ", "->", " ", "mp"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
              "1"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"ls", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "*", 
       "\n", "      ", 
       RowBox[{"wick", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Pick", "[", 
          RowBox[{"ls", ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"xo", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<x\>\""}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"po", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<p\>\""}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Length", "@", "ls"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"gExp", "[", "e_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Expand", "[", 
     RowBox[{"nc", "[", "e", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"m", " ", ":", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
         "_NonCommutativeMultiply", " ", "|", " ", "_GeneralizedPower"}], 
         ")"}]}], " ", ":>", " ", 
       RowBox[{"monExp", "[", 
        RowBox[{"letters", "@", "m"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"xo", " ", "->", " ", "mx"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"po", " ", "->", " ", "mp"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e3094245-7967-42b2-b7b1-99f23c76df6c"],

Cell["\<\
Test it on a mixed moment and a pure power, to see both the noncommuting \
piece and the Gaussian factorization:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"29955a0e-956c-489e-a87e-5822849b54ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"gExp", "[", 
    RowBox[{"xo", " ", "**", " ", "po"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gExp", "[", 
    RowBox[{"xo", " ", "**", " ", "xo", " ", "**", " ", "xo"}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"020d0151-5ea4-4c2d-b34e-545aed728084"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As expected, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "+", 
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6fe92c7-e09c-4a42-af66-853a58d53bfc"],
 ", with the imaginary part exactly the commutator's contribution, and the \
third moment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "3"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "3"], "+", "3", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e279efb2-0f4c-47b9-8106-123734331760"],
 " has no independent content, which is what \"Gaussian\" means. The \
pattern-dispatched ",
 Cell[BoxData["letters"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d9ccaf07-73af-444d-828f-2895c5609830"],
 " is doing the whole job of walking the canonical monomials, and it never \
has to know how they were ordered, because the algebra already ordered them."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bf6e8401-c24d-44dc-a8d1-0d4056ad652f"],

Cell["The Conditional Variances: The Noise Cancels", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"019df389-9a2c-4209-a3ac-d1289af0ea4d"],

Cell["\<\
Now the payoff. The general rule for how any observable evolves under the \
stochastic equation is\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4fa95abd-fecb-4814-a16b-daa5f23b3582"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["O", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["O", "TI"], "^"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["[",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["O", "TI"], "^"]}], 
       StyleBox["]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["O", "TI"], "^"], "}"}]}], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["W", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"e6fbff24-4a23-40b1-\
88fa-017a303c459d"],

Cell["\<\
In other words, an observable picks up a deterministic piece from the \
Hamiltonian, a second deterministic piece from the measurement, and a random \
piece proportional to how strongly it correlates with position. Encode that \
drift operator and that noise operator as two rules:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bac24b5d-137e-40de-9f25-770039c40de6"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"sseDrift", ",", " ", "sseNoise"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"sseDrift", "[", 
    RowBox[{"o_", ",", " ", "h_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"I", "/", "\[HBar]"}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
      RowBox[{"h", ",", " ", "o"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
      RowBox[{"xo", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"comm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"xo", ",", " ", "o"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"sseNoise", "[", "o_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]", "]"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"xo", " ", "**", " ", "o"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"o", " ", "**", " ", "xo"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"407fbf04-767d-4413-8e64-51ea1862beca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Remember that It\[OHat] calculus adds a cross term to every product, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a4d06da5-c697-470e-856b-2c02c673539f"],
 ". Apply the rules to the five moments that close on themselves for a free \
particle, take their Gaussian expectations, and assemble the three variance \
equations, showing drift and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708c0bd-ae95-4b32-aa5b-14674a8f665d"],
 "-coefficient side by side:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4ed85584-075e-444b-8379-235eef1815da"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"obs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"xo", ",", " ", "po", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"xo", " ", "**", " ", "xo"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"po", " ", "**", " ", "po"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"xo", " ", "**", " ", "po"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"po", " ", "**", " ", "xo"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"drift", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gExp", "[", 
      RowBox[{"sseDrift", "[", 
       RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"po", " ", "**", " ", "po"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "m"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
     " ", "obs"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"noise", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gExp", "[", 
        RowBox[{"sseNoise", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]", "]"}], " ", "mx", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gExp", "[", "#", "]"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
    " ", "obs"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"dmx", ",", " ", "dmp"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"drift", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{";;", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"nmx", ",", " ", "nmp"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"noise", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{";;", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Simplify", " ", "@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<dVx\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"drift", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "mx", " ", "dmx"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"nmx", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"noise", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "mx", " ", "nmx"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<dC \>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"drift", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "5", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mx", " ", "dmp"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mp", " ", "dmx"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"nmx", " ", "nmp"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"noise", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "5", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mx", " ", "nmp"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mp", " ", "nmx"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<dVp\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"drift", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "mp", " ", "dmp"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"nmp", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"noise", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "mp", " ", "nmp"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], " ", "//",
   " ", "TableForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3bae0ee4-f29c-42fd-8345-ed82989705af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Have you noticed something interesting? The third column, the coefficient \
of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47f591d7-c4ae-4aa2-9b7d-a19688773997"],
 ", is zero in all three rows. The means ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78acdc01-d385-4a4f-8243-4ed5c3314c25"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8308cde3-72de-4a03-a05d-331f7f89c3c6"],
 " wander randomly, but the ",
 StyleBox["conditional variances are completely deterministic", "TI"],
 ": they obey ordinary differential equations,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bf2cdfe3-35ba-48ba-88bd-8bdf68f51478"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["V", "TI"], "."], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["C", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "-", "4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], "."], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "-", 
     RowBox[{"4", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["V", "TI"], "."], 
     StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "-", "4", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f88e64b1-0edd-42b1-\
9f35-0e68221780cf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, every experimental run produces a differently-placed wave \
packet, but all of them have the identical width at the identical time. That \
is a strong and very checkable prediction, and in Part V we will check it to \
fourteen digits. Note also that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e6bcc3a7-058a-4806-970a-ca8b9bbd53d8"],
 " has zero drift, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ab3f90ff-2dd6-4427-8dcc-277acb37afd1"],
 " is a martingale: momentum information is not created by watching position, \
only shuffled between runs."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ac269360-3ee9-487d-9f8a-80ca6c5d3291"],

Cell["The Steady State: Where Localization and Spreading Balance", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"42ae55c0-bd42-45bb-bb36-667252a3eceb"],

Cell["\<\
The Riccati system has a fixed point. Find it, keeping everything symbolic:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a43ab719-9a1c-4da2-80fe-68789c8e6645"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fx", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Select", "[", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"2", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Cc", "/", "m"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Vx", "^", "2"}]}]}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Vp", "/", "m"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "Cc", " ", "Vx"}]}], " ", "==",
            " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
              RowBox[{"4", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Cc", "^", "2"}]}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}]}],
          "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"Vx", ",", " ", "Cc", ",", " ", "Vp"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"TrueQ", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"Vx", " ", "/.", " ", "#"}], ")"}], " ", ">", " ", "0"}],
            " ", "&&", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"Vp", " ", "/.", " ", "#"}], ")"}], " ", ">", " ", 
            "0"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
           RowBox[{"m", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], " ", 
       "&"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "Vx", "]"}], ",", " ", "Cc", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "Vp", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Vx", " ", "Vp"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Cc", "^", "2"}]}]}], "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", "fx"}], ",", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"m", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[11]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7912b8fe-4363-4a58-b395-1faa8b5d05e6"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, a continuously watched free particle relaxes to a wave packet \
of fixed width\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6eb898c6-981d-4cc6-96bd-2c46476d5767"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox["1", 
     SqrtBox["2"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      FractionBox["\[HBar]", 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "m"}], "TI"]], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4aeb585d-2e96-467f-\
85f2-4adf7fc8126b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and the last entry says ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cad0317b-6585-4669-9985-8f821c3a88a7"],
 " exactly: the packet is a ",
 StyleBox["minimum-uncertainty", "TI"],
 " state. Spreading and localization do not merely balance on average, they \
balance so precisely that the residual uncertainty is saturated. This is the \
quantitative content of the statement that measurement makes a particle \
classical, and it is the single most useful formula in this document, because \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a62ddf-e441-4008-a2c6-2c7c4150cd31"],
 " is what your spatial grid has to resolve."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"590c3eb7-1287-4d5e-a42d-90ca2d3c5820"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Check the two limits that must hold. Watching infinitely hard should pin \
the particle; the classical limit should too, since ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ea7c09bc-6dd1-447f-b7d7-26b33dc5076b"],
 " sets the scale of the residual spread:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f8bbe8ba-ac5b-4b87-9dc0-594586c3867a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Vx", " ", "/.", " ", "fx"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Vx", " ", "/.", " ", "fx"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Vx", " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"First", "@", 
     RowBox[{"DSolve", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Vx", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Cc", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "m"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Cc", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Vp", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "m"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Vp", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", 
         "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Vx", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "v0"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Cc", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Vp", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"4", " ", "v0"}], ")"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"Vx", ",", " ", "Cc", ",", " ", "Vp"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       "t"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[12]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5f7010b3-fb93-4b79-8c2a-d2679b304d7b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Therefore ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bc8467a5-d60d-4384-89a6-77cf6f6704de"],
 " in both the Zeno limit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e460e8db-bcdc-406d-92fa-3e25e2475fa3"],
 " and the classical limit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ed7e00b-725c-4471-bc61-e4d632df2626"],
 ", and at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d4d52d3-257c-4232-8cbf-4abd0b7d279a"],
 " the same Riccati system with the measurement switched off returns textbook \
free spreading, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "0"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], "0"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cc2ccfa2-53f6-40b7-8d25-7519163ad2d7"],
 ". Note that I extracted the solution by ",
 StyleBox["name", "TI"],
 " rather than by position: ",
 Cell[BoxData["DSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "013b21e3-75a6-486b-9d84-3a13245fb97c"],
 " returns its rules alphabetically, so here they arrive as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Cc", ",", " ", "Vp", ",", " ", "Vx"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9bf2abca-6e21-49d6-a427-93ab3ab1dd26"],
 " and indexing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e363845e-7bb0-4693-aed0-48ce70f9ce11"],
 " would silently hand you ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39c5955a-f0e3-4475-911d-42d3b9680615"],
 " while you believe you are holding ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d07f8fc4-9def-46ba-99a0-be0c5ff9c4ae"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"87860b65-f89b-4f24-9cfd-ea9a1fe411c5"],

Cell["\<\
Before we move on to the simulation, let us summarize what we have \
established exactly, with no numerics at all:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"279e669d-1353-494e-aa4c-1035d6d8310a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Gaussian Kraus family ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Proportional]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e37b9fda-d19c-4f19-92de-38fcfdbce02a"],
 " is complete, and its outcome law is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b00492c9-d09c-46bf-aca4-c1ca08cb9040"],
 " blurred by a Gaussian of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8d8786d6-79c0-4946-958c-9067372144e9"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fdea718f-4295-482b-aa31-4b1a259ad806"],

Cell["\<\
The stochastic equation preserves the norm identically, for any Hamiltonian \
and any measured observable, in any dimension.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5089f855-fa16-499a-8068-34d64a0f0853"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ensemble heating rate is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "\|01d53c", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fc92e183-2204-497b-871e-2db28071187b"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bf97ef55-875b-4333-aec3-986885796750"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The conditional variances are deterministic: all three ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b3a8a57c-dad4-4e5d-b0f3-4ac625aea5eb"],
 " coefficients vanish identically."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"73184790-4145-4e88-b3f0-db5cdc2f406a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The steady state is a minimum-uncertainty packet, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c3598e57-571d-461f-a3b2-253bda41aacd"],
 ", of width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e56c3bce-7856-4570-a7d0-fb029d6a53b8"],
 ", approached at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "/", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "83ff2447-fab6-4ec5-94a7-6046bc1c5dbf"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b9a26a0c-61d3-4ded-ac11-539943d6661b"],

Cell["\<\
Every one of those is a trap laid for the simulation we are about to write.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ea273d47-5f49-4be9-8b72-66ba09a597ba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part III: The Right Shelf Is ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "515ab178-4356-46ab-81e5-6a4224d23b14"]
}], "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0bad0cc4-3ebc-42b9-9b7a-d94d303159e2"],

Cell["Motivation by Failure: The Solver That Cannot See the Noise", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6dfcf910-feec-4f04-a088-41452f53b2a9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The reflex, faced with a differential equation in Wolfram Language, is ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7beaac42-2f98-458a-b0d7-422e42b52ddd"],
 ". Let us find out what happens, rather than assume:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9c879e5e-0267-4efa-84b2-7e7b9013e5e2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", 
       RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", 
        RowBox[{"w", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
    "  ", "x", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[13]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a551f440-5611-41c9-9b42-e5dcf5165c6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, this fails with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", "::", "underdet"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a453824-84bb-44b9-bf4c-4cf34ada9fca"],
 ", and the message is more informative than a simple refusal: it reports \
\"more dependent variables, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"w", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c8aab148-5d47-4a14-ba1c-aefa03993afe"],
 ", than equations.\" ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a29232e-29da-43f6-be11-1fda0b72e977"],
 " has parsed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "w"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107c9458-0d5b-4ed2-9fc8-9b586b109dbe"],
 " as a ",
 StyleBox["second unknown function", "TI"],
 " to be solved for, because nothing in its model of the world says ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["w", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a81160d-20ee-4265-bf21-6ad9b99e6e2d"],
 " is a stochastic process. A stochastic differential equation is not a \
differential equation with an extra term; it is a different object, and it \
lives on a different shelf."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0b476188-0800-42da-8dea-d793c0400d1d"],

Cell["Units and the Kinetic Operator: Setting the Numerical Stage", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"1f614244-be9e-4f3d-b38e-22d6fed3aacb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The right shelf is ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "93a3d68d-e92b-4b9a-a5b5-fdd9ce62be85"],
 ", which does know what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "w"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f11b9da0-4f03-440a-8293-31e2a5f0cf77"],
 " means. Everything from here on is numeric, so fix units ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8f0806f7-bbb1-477f-8164-5f479131aab1"],
 "; the symbolic scalings of Part II now take numbers:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"031d33a7-9f86-4163-afc2-df048b353495"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"mass", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[14]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5244affd-d6b3-4ad0-8e09-a12ac5b9ba8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To feed the equation to ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f2aefe15-9687-4f7f-b79e-c004c109cdad"],
 " we discretize position on a grid and need the kinetic operator on that \
grid. A finite-difference second derivative with periodic wrap keeps it \
local, hence sparse. Define it as a function of the grid size and spacing:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"55bdbfc3-05ba-48a1-bceb-1da31e1e9345"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "fdKinetic", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"fdKinetic", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "dx_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dx", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
     RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"i_", ",", " ", "i_"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"-", "2."}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"i_", ",", " ", "j_"}], "}"}], " ", "/;", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
             RowBox[{"i", " ", "-", " ", "j"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
            "1"}]}], " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "1."}]}], 
        "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[15]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"74f7a462-7c4e-4c13-b158-52cadc7d668c"],

Cell["\<\
The Grid SSE as an It\[OHat] Process: A Real State With Scalar Noise\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d051116a-75e6-4cde-ab16-75a798268d89"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the model itself. We represent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c619390-3d5e-4ceb-b6d1-93b833851955"],
 " by the real and imaginary parts of its grid values, stack them into one \
real state vector, and write the whole stochastic equation as a real \
It\[OHat] system driven by a single scalar Wiener process:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6ef4ff79-65a7-4171-94ae-501b225ec0a1"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "gridProcess", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"gridProcess", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "n_", ",", " ", "ll_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]0_"}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "dx", ",", " ", "xs", ",", " ", "kmat", ",", " ", "us", ",", " ", "vs", 
       ",", " ", "xav", ",", " ", "a", ",", " ", "drift", ",", " ", "diff"}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"dx", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ll", "/", "n"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"xs", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dx", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"kmat", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"fdKinetic", "[", 
        RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "dx"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"us", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Unique", "[", "\"\<u\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]}], 
      ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"vs", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Unique", "[", "\"\<v\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]}], 
      ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"xav", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"xs", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"us", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"vs", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"xs", " ", "-", " ", "xav"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"drift", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"kmat", " ", ".", " ", "vs"}], "/", "\[HBar]"}], " ", "-", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"a", "^", "2"}], " ", "us"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", 
            RowBox[{"kmat", " ", ".", " ", "us"}]}], "/", "\[HBar]"}], " ", "-",
           " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"a", "^", "2"}], " ", "vs"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"diff", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]", "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"a", " ", "us"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"a", " ", "vs"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"ItoProcess", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"drift", ",", " ", "diff"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
           RowBox[{"us", ",", " ", "vs"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Re", "@", "\[Psi]0"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Im", "@", "\[Psi]0"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[16]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a409e6a8-b270-438e-b9fd-fb09ce689dcb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two idioms here earn their place. The state variables come from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Unique", "[", "\"\<u\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9b0423bb-e756-4848-8336-2aa9a92f5eda"],
 ", which makes genuine plain symbols: ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4aae1e8e-b05a-4493-82d4-9dac94820e7e"],
 " insists on symbols, not indexed expressions like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"u", "[", "1", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "376dc264-f693-464f-8966-338c7e757ebb"],
 ", and feeding it the latter triggers a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Function", "::", "flpar"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f559362-86ab-496b-b144-9575f28af608"],
 " complaint. And the diffusion is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Times]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cce37fd0-634c-4c56-a7c1-0fab21526b04"],
 " matrix, a real state driven by a single scalar noise, which is exactly the \
shape that unlocks ",
 Cell[BoxData["RandomFunction"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "995a4863-68d0-49f2-bfcf-be77e637f04f"],
 "'s highest-order scalar-noise integrator."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01d2e4da-08aa-4fab-9765-3b38a8e1c7fb"],

Cell["The Position Grid: Reading the Momentum Ordering Aloud", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e5e45f9f-52bd-4364-bc26-f36bb3991a20"],

Cell["\<\
We also need a periodic position grid and a way to put a Gaussian wave packet \
on it. The grid carries both the positions and the FFT-ordered momenta the \
kinetic Fourier step will want later. Define both:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"09207ff5-8d3a-4bcb-8ef8-d26b06834d62"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"grid", ",", " ", "gaussian"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "ll_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dx", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ll", "/", "n"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<n\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "n"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<dx\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "dx"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dx", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
       "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<p\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "ll"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"RotateLeft", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "x0_", ",", " ", "p0_", ",", " ", "s_"}], "]"}], 
   " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"w", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "x0"}], 
             ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"4", " ", 
            RowBox[{"s", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"I", " ", "p0", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "/", "\[HBar]"}]}]}], 
        "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"w", "/", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"w", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "w", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[17]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"8d9a5662-e805-4456-85bc-e76e2ac9a76d"],

Cell["\<\
Look at the momentum list on a small grid before trusting it anywhere:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"59b155e4-5ccb-4b1d-b79e-ba8290d9c448"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
   RowBox[{"8", ",", " ", "4."}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[18]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e14723a4-6452-44e1-92bf-5d063eefadbd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the momenta are not in ascending order: they run ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", ",", 
   RowBox[{"+", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"+", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"+", "3"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ceb8721-f6d8-4daa-bdc9-d5452861916b"],
 " then wrap to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", "4"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e55e45d-f76f-4ff5-9a1c-c92dad090a51"],
 ", in units of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed20b66a-f7a1-4825-a3ef-f32caee5c403"],
 ". That scrambled order is the convention ",
 Cell[BoxData["Fourier"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9396b5e0-4615-4fda-ab3f-b5e5736476ac"],
 " expects, with the negative frequencies in the second half, and the ",
 Cell[BoxData["RotateLeft"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "85ed3728-a2cb-4dde-bb42-e11ebe77f05c"],
 " is what places our physical momenta into it. Getting this ordering wrong \
is the classic way a spectral kinetic step runs without error and propagates \
the packet in the wrong direction."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"06ee3596-b886-47e5-af9b-e49468ddf2b5"],

Cell["\<\
A Trajectory You Can Watch: One Run of the Built-In Integrator\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"0cbdefe0-1dd1-4a29-92e3-eaea728701e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With the process and the grid in hand, we need only to read a trajectory \
back. A raw ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01d2d2cd-0b5d-44d4-b4ac-73e0208ae2ef"],
 " sample is a real state vector; reassemble it into a wavefunction and read \
off the conditional mean position:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0e29a74b-ac9e-460e-8fdd-69784f2a2501"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"stateTo\[Psi]", ",", " ", "condX"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"stateTo\[Psi]", "[", "s_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Length", "[", "s", "]"}], "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"s", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{";;", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", 
       RowBox[{"s", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], " ", ";;"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"condX", "[", 
    RowBox[{"s_", ",", " ", "xs_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{"stateTo\[Psi]", "[", "s", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], "}"}],
      ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"xs", " ", ".", " ", "p"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"Total", "[", "p", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[19]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"42decb65-4577-4094-ba94-e24d73af77c4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now simulating is one call to ",
 Cell[BoxData["RandomFunction"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "716b8234-9c07-4845-b92b-e58e66d8682a"],
 ", which returns a ",
 Cell[BoxData["TemporalData"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "22f367de-f254-4ef4-9c03-091554696630"],
 " object carrying every path. Evolve one free trajectory and watch the \
conditional mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201ac071-6bc0-4c67-98c5-43c1330d2522"],
 " random-walk as the detector localizes the packet:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6b12eb00-0ad7-4f7e-84b1-436bc02a4d9b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "32"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ll", " ", "=", " ", "16."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "3."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.002"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xs", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"ll", "/", "n"}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"td", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"RandomFunction", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"gridProcess", "[", 
         RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "ll", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
             RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "ll"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
            "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "dt"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
        "Method", " ", "->", 
         " ", "\"\<StochasticRungeKuttaScalarNoise\>\""}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}],
    ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"td", "[", "\"\<Times\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"condX", "[", 
           RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "xs"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"td", "[", "\"\<ValueList\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "480"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<\[LeftAngleBracket]x\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
     "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<One conditional trajectory: \[LeftAngleBracket]x\
\[RightAngleBracket] wanders as the packet localizes\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[20]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"f46e574e-4e8a-4de6-8eac-9e1ebb549646"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That plot is the single most important picture in continuous measurement: a \
pure state, conditioned on the noisy measurement record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d6a1a521-1f6e-4379-b32b-b90a64bef522"],
 ", whose center wanders while its width collapses to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4bcad061-1576-45a1-9dbf-ab65d9cc85b1"],
 ". The built-in stochastic machinery produced it with no integrator written \
by hand."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9a0dbb88-11f7-4dd3-b0fc-fbbf13affb68"],

Cell["\<\
The Ensemble Reproduces the Lindblad Equation: Two Routes That Must Agree\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b5b4fe6b-b097-4141-aab4-266b2e9add8e"],

Cell["\<\
The defining property of the whole construction is that averaging the \
trajectories must reproduce the Lindblad equation. Test it against a \
completely different computational route, the matrix exponential of the \
Liouvillian, so that agreement is evidence and not tautology:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"03c7a764-6c25-4c86-a6f2-34874fa1b7ca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "24"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ll", " ", "=", " ", "12."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "0.4"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.0005"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntraj", " ", "=", " ", "400"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "ll"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xm", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kmat", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"fdKinetic", "[", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ll", "/", "n"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"id", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "n", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Psi]0", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "1.2", ",", " ", "0.9"}], 
       "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x2ito", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
         RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"With", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
                RowBox[{"stateTo\[Psi]", "@", "s"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], 
             "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", 
              " ", "p"}], "/", 
             RowBox[{"Total", "[", "p", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "/@", 
        "\n", "      ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"RandomFunction", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"gridProcess", "[", 
             RowBox[{
             "n", ",", " ", "ll", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", 
              "\[Psi]0"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "dt"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
            "ntraj", ",", "\n", "         ", 
            RowBox[{
            "Method", " ", "->", 
             " ", "\"\<StochasticRungeKuttaScalarNoise\>\""}]}], "]"}], 
          "[", "\"\<ValueList\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"rhoL", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ArrayReshape", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"tf", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", "\n", "        ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"I", "/", "\[HBar]"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"kmat", ",", " ", "id"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"id", ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"Transpose", "@", "kmat"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], 
             "\n", "        ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"xm", " ", ".", " ", "xm"}], ",", " ", "id"}], 
                 "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"xm", ",", " ", "xm"}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
                "           ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"id", ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"xm", " ", ".", " ", "xm"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
            ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
          RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
           RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "\[Psi]0", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Conjugate", "@", "\[Psi]0"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
        "     ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<<x^2> ensemble\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<<x^2> Lindblad\>\"", ",",
        " ", "\"\<rel. diff\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Monte-Carlo scale\>\""}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x2ito", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"rhoL", " ", ".", " ", "xm", " ", ".", " ", "xm"}], "]"}]}], 
       ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x2ito", "/", 
          RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
            RowBox[{"rhoL", " ", ".", " ", "xm", " ", ".", " ", "xm"}], 
            "]"}]}]}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "ntraj", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[21]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"244d19f6-cdaf-422c-ad40-bc0f7c077d4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the ensemble average agrees with the Lindblad reference up \
to Monte-Carlo scatter. Do not expect it to hit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["ntraj",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b25f8d5-0e5b-4172-b6fb-045b4c0d6377"],
 " exactly: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "97548bca-3f28-4cca-81f8-ef176a937b06"],
 " is a variance-like estimator with a broader sampling distribution than the \
mean, so at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["ntraj",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "=", "400"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ca8e699c-6bdf-4be1-9a58-97b192ad2523"],
 " a few percent is normal. Push ",
 Cell[BoxData["ntraj"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e7d2cae1-c220-440f-93ec-266971ed1ad9"],
 " up and the gap closes. The built-in route is correct."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"496e17cc-1fa0-4c1d-94dc-343ec6c316f0"],

Cell["Why the Library Route Is Not the End: Two Visible Symptoms", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b422d1ce-3ff4-4f5e-9bb9-4b2733f3e40f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50122ed4-a6b8-4bab-b57b-ef8ded017549"],
 " gives a correct, honest simulation with essentially no bespoke code. Why \
write anything more? Two reasons, and both are visible symptoms rather than \
opinions."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e32addec-769c-44b8-bb80-2efd3aaee2a3"],

Cell["\<\
The first is that a general SDE integrator does not know our equation \
preserves the norm, so it does not. Read the norm-squared at the start and \
the end of a run:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d63f9486-de11-48cd-8520-a491b0bd9b2f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "32"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ll", " ", "=", " ", "16."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "=", " ", "3."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.002"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"td", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"RandomFunction", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gridProcess", "[", 
        RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "ll", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
            RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "ll"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
           "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "dt"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
       "Method", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<StochasticRungeKuttaScalarNoise\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"td", "[", "\"\<ValueList\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"td", "[", "\"\<ValueList\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[22]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"136ade2f-8425-4565-a9a8-ecd446196619"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The norm-squared starts at ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba0bb255-3e58-4a42-8601-e095056c0754"],
 " and drifts, and the drift grows with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bdd5d9db-155c-40de-80e3-bd7b9a18cc46"],
 ", with the step size, and with time. You can renormalize by hand after each \
step, but that patches the symptom."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f98d968b-515e-4a4f-ba18-eb603c674483"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The deeper reason is the second one, and Part V will make it quantitative: \
the coefficients of this equation are ",
 StyleBox["unbounded", "TI"],
 " in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "83572ae3-dfee-4db8-b774-f40062c1bd02"],
 ", the drift carrying ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a1645744-6c83-4a41-866e-1340e0acc302"],
 ", and an explicit scheme applied to an unbounded generator is not \
unconditionally stable. The exponential of that generator is. That is the \
structural fact the next part exploits, and it is the difference between a \
simulation that runs and one you can trust to fourteen digits."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3054815f-a10a-4967-b911-a97315e6d528"],

Cell["Part IV: A Propagator That Exponentiates the Measurement", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"89efced0-e1fc-4867-b9b4-810b5a8f6052"],

Cell["Diagonal in Position: The One Fact That Picks the Integrator", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"987e22bf-18ce-4b2e-a5bb-ead91d9492ee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Look again at the equation and ask what kind of operators appear. The \
Hamiltonian mixes positions and momenta. But ",
 StyleBox["every measurement term", "TI"],
 ", both the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9e4ea67e-933d-45c9-9d7e-b29a193bcb80"],
 " drift and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb4718b7-b83c-4568-8467-ca5c8a778cb1"],
 " noise, is a multiplication operator in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ebd8eb7-2ac7-40e2-ae39-c4af071c0ba9"],
 ". On a position grid it is a diagonal matrix, or simply a list you multiply \
pointwise."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8f10dc43-320e-4fa8-b54c-d346e97d9218"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is not a cosmetic observation, it is the whole method. Because the \
measurement terms commute among themselves, the measurement channel over a ",
 StyleBox["finite", "TI"],
 " interval is exactly the Gaussian Kraus operator we started from: two \
measurements of strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60759ba8-6be3-4618-89e2-c9c43acceff5"],
 " compose exactly into one of strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dac29518-001e-4685-9436-ce725aca51ee"],
 ". So a scheme that applies the measurement as a Kraus multiplication \
carries ",
 StyleBox["no discretization error at all from the measurement",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", at any step size, and multiplies by the bounded factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05031d47-7162-4589-a70b-de01b4f6b4e1"],
 " rather than the unbounded ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "-", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8859a196-5ee5-4cd6-84c8-8b27815e6d4a"],
 ". The only error left is the failure of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "84c59265-acd2-4aa4-a9b6-c466d117a5c5"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b672754d-00c8-4a39-90b6-af9e8cde6f18"],
 " to commute."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"784aa29f-040b-45f4-b9ee-cf5d2fa74921"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Equivalently: the equation is telling you how to integrate it. Split off \
the part you can do exactly, and spend your step size only on the part you \
cannot. The lesson that transfers to any problem is the question, not the \
answer: ",
 StyleBox["which part of my generator can I exponentiate exactly?", "TI"]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4d46c562-59b1-4fc3-a534-55334916a57b"],

Cell["The Moment Readouts: One Line Each", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"73a9677f-1b9e-42db-add8-146cbab43b63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We will need to read ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a82f575f-7142-43bb-88cc-d4a25c5b78c2"],
 ", the conditional variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64646674-07f8-4990-b9ae-19329f8dfd3d"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a389326-701a-40b9-8814-4038984a203a"],
 " off a grid wavefunction. Position moments are dot products against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "079a88f5-fe26-4c6e-94b9-482b9c9f70ce"],
 "; the momentum moment goes through the Fourier transform. Define the \
three:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"54ef4916-c2d2-401a-bee2-2d22a2779370"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"xExp", ",", " ", "vxOf", ",", " ", "p2Exp"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xExp", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xExp", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Psi]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"p2Exp", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[23]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"aacbf5ae-4758-455d-92a7-5bd52499481c"],

Cell["\<\
The Unitary Substeps: Kinetic in Fourier, Potential Pointwise\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b10bd1e3-305e-4130-8ae4-17b9d78df215"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We represent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ac7040df-8266-4f7e-8934-291b04413406"],
 " on a uniform periodic grid, so the kinetic term is a multiplication in the \
Fourier domain and the potential term is a pointwise phase. Each is a curried \
operator: give it the grid and the step size and it returns a function that \
maps a wavefunction to a wavefunction:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"efa14842-ec42-432e-8a18-9bbfd83a57a2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"kinStep", ",", " ", "potStep"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"kinStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"InverseFourier", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"dt", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "\[HBar]"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"potStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "pot_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_",
     "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "pot", " ", 
      RowBox[{"dt", "/", "\[HBar]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "\[Psi]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[24]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3a601cb6-8002-49e8-87d3-4aa4e9637fa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That currying is what will let us compose the substeps without an explicit \
loop. I will not ask you to trust that the Fourier convention is right; \
propagate a free Gaussian and compare against the closed-form spreading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "0", "2"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["s", "TI"], "0"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7de860f1-3fba-41cc-bc8b-b6d04867aaf9"],
 " from Part II:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f702d381-4cc3-4704-95d0-77e021550563"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
       RowBox[{"512", ",", " ", "60."}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"s0", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"p0", " ", "=", " ", "1.5"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]T", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"kinStep", "[", 
        RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"tf", "/", "400"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
        RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "5."}], ",", " ", "p0", ",", " ", "s0"}], "]"}], ",", 
       " ", "400"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Vx exact\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Vx grid\>\"", ",", 
       " ", "\"\<<x> exact\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<<x> grid\>\""}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"s0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", 
           RowBox[{"tf", "/", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "s0"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], "^", 
         "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
        RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Psi]T"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "5."}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"p0", " ", 
         RowBox[{"tf", "/", "mass"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"xExp", "[", 
        RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Psi]T"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[25]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ceff24e3-e116-4f83-b5d6-990842310c13"],

Cell["\<\
The variance matches the closed form to thirteen digits and the packet has \
moved to the right, which is the check that actually matters: a sign error in \
the Fourier convention would send it left while leaving the variance \
perfectly correct. Whenever you validate a propagator, test something that \
the error you fear would actually break.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0677ec2c-946c-46dd-8063-3956293365d0"],

Cell["The Measurement Substep: Exponentiate the Backaction", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"0b0008dc-d202-4dbd-a8fe-405f78bde6db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The measurement step is the whole quantum backaction of watching the \
particle. Draw an outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "de7f11c7-7125-402f-bb92-4068c839c345"],
 " from the exact outcome law of Part I, then multiply pointwise by the \
Gaussian Kraus factor and renormalize:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c2cb5d9e-682f-4dab-8129-819f0f65fd29"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"drawExact", ",", " ", "measStep"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", 
    "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
     RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
     "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"measStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", 
    "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"xb", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", 
        "\[Psi]", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "\[Lambda]"}], " ", "dt", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "xb"}], 
            ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "\[Psi]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"v", "/", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"v", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "v", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[26]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"8c5f2f14-509f-4d6d-a28d-23ae9fda69db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That Kraus factor can only ever damp the wavefunction, never amplify it. \
Keep that boundedness in mind: in Part V it is the reason this scheme is \
stable and the explicit one is not. Before composing anything, sample the \
detector readings ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b54ac39-ab3a-481e-bc85-ea053d000975"],
 " directly and check them against the outcome law of Part I, closing the \
factor-of-two worry by sampling rather than by algebra:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5c6b328c-0df6-42bf-9646-18b421553aca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
       RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "40."}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]0", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "0.7", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}]}],
     "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"draws", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", 
        "\[Psi]0", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "200000", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<mean predicted\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<mean sampled\>\"", ",",
        " ", "\"\<variance predicted\>\"", ",", 
       " ", "\"\<variance sampled\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"xExp", "[", 
        RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Psi]0"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "draws", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Psi]0"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"1", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Variance", "[", "draws", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[27]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5faff5a7-bf45-4b03-91ae-0d610386629a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the sampled mean lands on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f221a16-85fe-4ef5-83cf-0df2db0e3a38"],
 " and the sampled variance on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "+", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1aa4fa31-bf65-4749-919c-6ff411d48a4c"],
 ", the conditional spread of the packet plus the detector's own blur. This \
is the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "da911da5-eac0-44e2-b9f6-82e183fbbd37"],
 " we carried symbolically in Part I, now confirmed by two hundred thousand \
draws."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c4cbef51-1f37-4624-b887-2dafb39d21d0"],

Cell["Assembling the Step: Composing Without a Loop", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b64dee0c-7878-479a-8c56-74c28189808f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A full step is a composition of substeps. ",
 Cell[BoxData["RightComposition"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6278427d-1bc7-4200-83f0-c6726c5ebd80"],
 " reads left-to-right in application order, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Nest"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9a0f4754-e992-4861-8360-8e7835df2b18"],
 " runs the trajectory, so there is no explicit iteration anywhere. Build the \
symmetric assembly, which splits the measurement in half and wraps it around \
the unitary step, together with a runner that iterates it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8ab9dcb1-c9a6-45ff-a6d3-e6a7d758861c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"stepSym", ",", " ", "evolve"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"stepSym", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "pot_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_"}],
     "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"RightComposition", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"measStep", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dt", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"potStep", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "pot", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dt", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kinStep", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"potStep", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "pot", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dt", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"measStep", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dt", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
     RowBox[{"step_", ",", " ", "tf_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", 
    "\[Psi]0_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
    RowBox[{"step", ",", " ", "\[Psi]0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
      RowBox[{"tf", "/", "dt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[28]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"f148e7ca-f201-4bfc-90d7-37a86cb3e3b7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two things have to be right about any experiment on this propagator, and I \
got both wrong on my first attempt. The first is ",
 StyleBox["when", "TI"],
 " to measure the steady state: the Riccati system relaxes at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "/", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "165d1485-c82a-460a-9950-da1ac16ec232"],
 ", so comparing too early plateaus on the transient rather than on the \
step-size error. We measure at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "8"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b68b594-23d3-4ff7-81ea-91f9ce39b6d2"],
 ", many relaxation times in. The second is ",
 StyleBox["how wide", "TI"],
 " the box must be: the conditional mean random-walks, and because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "700b3700-8075-45cc-92c0-98b6da289816"],
 " random-walks too and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a07c9ac-aedf-4f91-818b-9013ef3ff232"],
 " integrates it, the spread grows like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "3"], "/", "3", "+", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2440e963-ddc4-416c-81be-0f069968e196"],
 ", not ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0da2b704-142c-48fa-9725-197170a8e463"],
 ". On a periodic box the packet must not wrap, because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d6c3ca4-a616-4898-b235-9651411fb4dd"],
 " is not periodic and wrapping corrupts ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b783d07d-3df4-48c1-a60b-55d1c4a8f416"],
 " silently. So the box is sized for the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "3"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c271ca6-fa80-412d-b85f-45fd9d7207d5"],
 " wander, not for the packet width."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e3939068-3321-4ec1-810f-cb2ec6caf329"],

Cell["\<\
With both settled, measure the order by comparing the naive assembly \
(measurement last) against the symmetric one:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c7221a1b-6791-41a4-8b50-9967da096f32"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
       RowBox[{"1024", ",", " ", "160."}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "8."}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]0", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"dt", ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
             RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"RightComposition", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"potStep", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"0.", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"dt", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"kinStep", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
                   "          ", 
                   RowBox[{"potStep", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"0.", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"dt", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"measStep", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], 
                    "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[",
                "\[Psi]0", "]"}]}], "]"}], "/", "0.5"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}],
           "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
             RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"stepSym", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"0.", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
                   "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "tf", ",", 
                 " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]0", "]"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
            "0.5"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"dt", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0.008", ",", " ", "0.004", ",", " ", "0.002"}], "}"}]}], 
        "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<dt\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<measurement last\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<symmetrised\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[29]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"fc6b28e0-3be1-4b2d-b831-0c8e167660f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Halving the step size halves the error in the first column but quarters it \
in the second: the naive assembly is first order and the symmetrized one is \
second order, for one extra random draw per step. The reason generalizes to \
every operator-splitting scheme you will ever write. Splitting error comes \
from the non-commutation of the pieces, and a ",
 StyleBox["symmetric", "TI"],
 " arrangement makes the leading commutator cancel between the two halves. \
Putting the measurement last leaves it unpaired."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"06eafd7f-0528-4f7d-b3eb-0a8550004430"],

Cell["The Record Is the Data, the State Is the Inference", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"852b16d9-b297-491a-b91e-6effef6f9412"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Everything simulated so far is the conditional state, and no laboratory has \
one. What an experiment produces is the sequence of readings ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062597ff-0b57-440b-9fa4-90a383db3b7c"],
 ", and the state is what you compute from them. ",
 Cell[BoxData["measStep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d51b41dc-60f3-40c5-bc65-ba7cd7b1cf9a"],
 " already draws that number and discards it. Keep it instead, by splitting \
the draw from the deterministic update it implies:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9ea527fb-9042-488a-a8de-5eaf079f3ceb"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"measAt", ",", " ", "stepAt", ",", " ", "filter"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"measAt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "xb_"}],
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "\[Lambda]"}], " ", "dt", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "xb"}], 
            ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "\[Psi]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"v", "/", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"v", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "v", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"stepAt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "xb_"}],
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"kinStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"measAt", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "xb"}], 
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"filter", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "rec_"}], "]"}],
     "[", "\[Psi]0_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"stepAt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "#2"}], 
        "]"}], "[", "#1", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "\[Psi]0", ",", " ", 
     "rec"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[30]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e6667c3c-0566-4c0b-b758-e9234e513c5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the finite-bin update of Part I applied literally: one reading per \
bin, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba37a9b1-358e-47af-b6bb-fbc5a6e7d83a"],
 " and then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "610d78b4-315c-403e-b50b-b22ae3a10c8e"],
 ". Once ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "890ce27b-d865-4be2-bbc1-3470c860e72d"],
 " is fixed, ",
 Cell[BoxData["stepAt"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f3bd707-ed4f-4fde-9b5e-3cd3b9f89129"],
 " contains no randomness at all, since ",
 Cell[BoxData["RandomChoice"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6f977ee-5b53-4e9f-9981-989a9f054c3c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["RandomVariate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60ed1683-c54d-43c0-8a85-acf982d77f14"],
 " live only in ",
 Cell[BoxData["drawExact"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c5029c1e-642e-49c9-917b-b3595c4cd492"],
 ". Experiment and inference are therefore two different traversals of the \
same step. The experiment draws its own readings and emits data; the filter \
consumes data and emits states, and it is a plain ",
 Cell[BoxData["FoldList"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cc9a2343-04d0-4d10-aa15-5a8c31dfcac7"],
 ", which is the whole content of quantum filtering."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3ca3c126-a5cb-4f32-853e-5222c7afaa41"],

Cell["\<\
Run one experiment. We keep its final state only so that the reconstruction \
can be checked against it, which is a luxury no experimentalist has:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"61b59ee6-98cd-41d5-a651-09ecf171e9a9"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "20260727", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gRec", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "40."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Lambda]Rec", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dtRec", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Psi]Rec", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gRec", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]End", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "rec", "}"}]}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Reap", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"With", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"xb", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
              RowBox[{"gRec", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]Rec", ",", " ", "dtRec"}], 
              "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sow", "[", "xb", "]"}], ";", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"stepAt", "[", 
             RowBox[{
             "gRec", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]Rec", ",", " ", "dtRec", ",", " ", 
              "xb"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      "\n", "   ", "\[Psi]Rec", ",", " ", "800"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[31]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"32c52335-693d-4ed3-9854-a8def7d1e0df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now reconstruct from ",
 Cell[BoxData["rec"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d732eb3a-9138-4735-85e4-d8b050c6f178"],
 " alone, both from the true initial state and from a deliberately wrong \
guess placed three units away with twice the width:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1dabb1cc-8f9e-4bb6-85eb-6d24f097dae6"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tru", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"filter", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "gRec", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]Rec", ",", " ", "dtRec", ",", " ", "rec"}], 
     "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]Rec", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gue", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"filter", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "gRec", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]Rec", ",", " ", "dtRec", ",", " ", "rec"}], 
     "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
     RowBox[{"gRec", ",", " ", "3.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<detector noise sd\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<packet width Sqrt[Vx]\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<signal to noise per reading\>\"", ",", "\n", 
     "  ", "\"\<replay error max|d\[Psi]|\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<overlap of wrong start with truth, initial\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<overlap, final\>\"", ",", "\n", 
     "  ", "\"\<Vx, true trajectory\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Vx, wrong start\>\"",
      ",", " ", "\"\<predicted Vx\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"1", "/", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]Rec", " ", "dtRec"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
      RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gRec", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Last", "@", "tru"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]Rec", " ", "dtRec", " ", 
       RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gRec", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Last", "@", "tru"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Last", "[", "tru", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "\[Psi]End"}], 
       "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", 
         RowBox[{"First", "@", "tru"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"First", "@", "gue"}]}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Last", "@", "tru"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Last", "@", "gue"}]}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gRec", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Last", "@", "tru"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gRec", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Last", "@", "gue"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]Rec", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[32]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"20e94691-16fa-483b-a2aa-666c365e19cf"],

Cell["\<\
Three things to read, in the order that matters for an experiment.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e80a3a32-2368-48d7-a57f-e0bb81c157c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The record is not the trajectory.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The detector noise has standard deviation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"4", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "\[TildeTilde]", "7.1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1c243b0-d35a-444e-b4ae-acea0cb6b5cb"],
 ", against a packet whose entire width is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "\[TildeTilde]", "0.71"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6feeb131-45a5-4d07-9240-969d9a18ff36"],
 ". One reading therefore carries a signal-to-noise ratio near ",
 Cell[BoxData["0.1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "daf4b3fc-a7f4-48f1-82c1-3f49c42b2bdd"],
 ", and that figure is a property of the detector rather than of the run: the \
wander of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41694ac8-679f-4873-aa28-9977ff96f14c"],
 " accumulates with time, so any ratio formed against it would depend only on \
how long you watched. The smooth curve plotted earlier is an inference and \
never an observation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"99dddf86-3d0d-418c-9401-ea5c726f6412"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The state is a deterministic function of the record.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The replay error is exactly zero, not merely small: feeding the readings \
back through ",
 Cell[BoxData["filter"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23efb35d-c9fb-4873-946b-8eaf1914313c"],
 " returns the original trajectory bit for bit. Every random number in the \
theory is spent producing the data, and none is left in the map from data to \
state."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5bc1ab3e-d54c-4862-9562-79f8f44571e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The filter forgets a wrong initial state.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Started from the wrong place and the wrong width, and fed the same \
readings, its overlap with the truth climbs from about ",
 Cell[BoxData["0.33"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8641190d-f877-40b8-8bc1-20e832b484c2"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData["0.9997"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b3a93b04-197e-4d07-ba22-b90b9834b808"],
 ", and its conditional variance agrees with the true trajectory's to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"7", "\[Times]", 
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "5"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cdf090f4-a01d-4b31-b9fe-43ea720ebba8"],
 ". Both then sit about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0.4", "%"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "acf54f43-a7cb-4283-9a0b-7319b7ed3c6e"],
 " above the analytic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"4", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b378ed28-52d1-4b98-8935-fd5eea3581d8"],
 ", which is the splitting error of this assembly rather than any failure of \
the filter: ",
 Cell[BoxData["stepAt"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c33ae3d4-a1f7-48c2-96ee-3e1bb502b60c"],
 " applies the measurement last, so it is the first-order scheme measured \
just above, and the gap falls to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0.04", "%"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6b8e0a1-fdd3-4452-929d-0224c16c7ef7"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "0.001"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b00bec4d-16bc-492a-8640-a20d591f8d32"],
 ". This is what makes the equation usable in a laboratory, where the initial \
state is exactly what you do not know."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"351f8e5d-c126-4c8b-a12c-fb2c6ab831d9"],

Cell["\<\
The relation is one picture: the data, and the single trajectory it \
determines.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13f54537-1c7b-4184-890b-9210dd25db1c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ListPlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dtRec", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Length", "@", "rec"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "rec"}], "}"}], 
      "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.35", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PointSize", "[", "0.004", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dtRec", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Length", "@", "rec"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"xExp", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gRec", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ",
          "tru"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", "Red"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Axes", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dtRec", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Length", "@", "rec"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "All"}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<reading, and the inferred mean\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<800 detector readings and the one trajectory they \
determine\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[33]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"911da5e5-5522-4921-9e56-0f7af7802d1a"],

Cell["Part V: Trusting the Answer", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"02975387-8019-4df9-aa32-484681082bba"],

Cell["\<\
A number produced by a simulation is a hypothesis. This part is the ladder \
that turns it into a result, and I have ordered the rungs by how much they \
can catch.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0e0d1f13-0595-4480-b94b-ddac1222f948"],

Cell["\<\
The Variances Are Deterministic: A Test With No Statistics In It\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"14d5570c-2266-456a-90d6-17a00614bfcf"],

Cell["\<\
Part II predicted that all runs share the identical conditional variance. \
That is an unusually sharp claim, because it needs no averaging at all: two \
runs with different noise must agree to machine precision. Run six \
independent trajectories on a fine grid and compare their widths:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a44b2e8e-30a1-44bf-997a-c07eb5e29126"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
       RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "40."}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.002"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"runs", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
        RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"stepSym", "[", 
             RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"0.", " ", 
               RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", 
              ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "4.", ",", " ", "dt"}], 
           "]"}], "[", 
          RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
           RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], 
           "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "6", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<values\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<spread across runs\>\"", ",", 
       " ", "\"\<predicted\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"runs", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "runs", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[34]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a5d0805e-4a47-4719-9104-0ec0040ebef8"],

Cell["\<\
Six different noise realizations agree to roughly fourteen digits while \
landing on the predicted steady width. This one test simultaneously confirms \
the Riccati derivation, the sampling law, and the propagator, and it does so \
without a single statistical error bar.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ffe55acc-be7b-458a-a684-9773fd851d3b"],

Cell["The Same Test Is Where the Library Route Shows Its Seams", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"96253b55-3b5b-4540-87cc-307933b2a627"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That sharpness gives us a clean way to see what the exact-Kraus step buys \
over the general integrator of Part III. The split-step keeps the state ",
 StyleBox["exactly", "TI"],
 " Gaussian, so its variance is deterministic. A general explicit integrator \
does not, so its variance both scatters across runs and drifts off the \
predicted value. Put the two side by side on the same grid:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"183e720f-4d00-493f-885a-6414c737eb77"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "32"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ll", " ", "=", " ", "16."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.002"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nrun", " ", "=", " ", "5"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "ll"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]0", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ss", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"stepSym", "[", 
              RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"0.", " ", 
                RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "\[Lambda]",
                ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "dt"}], 
            "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]0", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "nrun", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"it\[Psi]s", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"stateTo\[Psi]", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"RandomFunction", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"gridProcess", "[", 
            RowBox[{
            "n", ",", " ", "ll", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "\[Psi]0"}],
             "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "dt"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           "nrun", ",", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{
           "Method", " ", "->", 
            " ", "\"\<StochasticRungeKuttaScalarNoise\>\""}]}], "]"}], 
         "[", "\"\<ValueList\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<split-step spread\>\"", ",", 
       " ", "\"\<ItoProcess spread\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<split mean\>\"", ",", 
       " ", "\"\<Ito mean\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<predicted\>\""}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "ss", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
           RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         "it\[Psi]s"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "ss", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"vxOf", "[", 
           RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         "it\[Psi]s"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[35]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"b7d2d1e4-a4b3-4b1c-982a-3e732b11098b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the same coarse grid, the split-step widths agree to a part in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["10", "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3421b495-d01a-4949-8b9c-6448081df2b1"],
 " (limited only by the discreteness of ",
 Cell[BoxData["RandomChoice"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69aa8396-6226-468d-a66d-4b3b2803f5ff"],
 " on ",
 Cell[BoxData["32"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "606ee232-a243-4a72-85ce-f92ff2fcf460"],
 " points) while the ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e2e1a46b-41a3-4398-a529-8f4de41ccd41"],
 " widths scatter by a thousand times more and sit biased below the predicted \
",
 Cell[BoxData["0.5"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d6b058c7-2123-4d42-93f5-d53b63034342"],
 ". Both routes are simulating the same equation. Only the one that \
exponentiates the measurement keeps the exact Gaussianity the physics \
guarantees. This is the concrete payoff of asking which part of the generator \
you can exponentiate."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"af9ea8bb-d227-42a8-8594-f7b6fcd99945"],

Cell["\<\
Two Representations Agree: The Trajectory Ensemble Against the Lindblad \
Equation\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"04cc4271-91a3-4d2d-b33c-846bc903fca0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We already saw the ensemble reproduce the Lindblad equation for the ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b38bb36e-7390-4fc7-a7a9-3ec51252c606"],
 " route in Part III. Confirm it holds for the split-step too, this time also \
watching purity fall as the ensemble decoheres while every single trajectory \
stays exactly pure. First the reference Hamiltonian as a matrix, built column \
by column from the spectral kinetic operator:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cbccd111-35c4-41bb-a227-0e6aa2823f5a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "kinMat", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"kinMat", "[", "g_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"InverseFourier", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
          RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<n\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[36]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6b297651-78ee-4fb7-85c7-00f8bfa7daa6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now build the Liouvillian, exponentiate it for the Lindblad reference, \
average three thousand split-step trajectories for the unravelling, and \
compare ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21bec594-0992-42a9-a83e-9730fc1b4f05"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f1f2b8f3-0dd2-45e0-9e76-957cc89796a5"],
 ", and the purity:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"44caffa1-5af0-4d34-ac71-1ee053d1d985"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"nn", " ", "=", " ", "32"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ll", " ", "=", " ", "12."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "0.4"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.0005"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntraj", " ", "=", " ", "3000"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
      RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", "ll"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"id", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "nn", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"xm", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"hm", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"kinMat", "[", "g", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Psi]0", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1."}], ",", " ", "1.2", ",", " ", "0.9"}], "]"}]}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"liou", ",", " ", "rhoL", ",", " ", "ens", ",", " ", "obs"}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"liou", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"I", "/", "\[HBar]"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
             RowBox[{"hm", ",", " ", "id"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
             RowBox[{"id", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "hm", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], "\n",
          "    ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"xm", " ", ".", " ", "xm"}], ",", " ", "id"}], "]"}], 
            " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", 
             RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
              RowBox[{"xm", ",", " ", "xm"}], "]"}]}], "\n", "       ", "+", 
            " ", 
            RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
             RowBox[{"id", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"xm", " ", ".", " ", "xm"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
        ")"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"rhoL", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ArrayReshape", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
           RowBox[{"liou", " ", "tf"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
           RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "\[Psi]0", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Conjugate", "@", "\[Psi]0"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"nn", ",", " ", "nn"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"ens", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Conjugate", "@", "#"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], "@", "\n",
            "       ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"stepSym", "[", 
               RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"0.", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
                "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "tf", ",", 
              " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]0", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "ntraj", "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"obs", "[", "r_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
          RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
           RowBox[{"r", " ", ".", " ", "xm"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
          RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
           RowBox[{"r", " ", ".", " ", "xm", " ", ".", " ", "xm"}], "]"}]}], ",",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
          RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
           RowBox[{"r", " ", ".", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "  ", 
      RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<<x>\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<<x^2>\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<purity\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"obs", "[", "rhoL", "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"obs", "[", "ens", "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"obs", "[", "ens", "]"}], "/", 
              RowBox[{"obs", "[", "rhoL", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], 
            "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<observable\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Lindblad\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<3000 trajectories\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<rel. diff\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[37]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"b113e9e2-801b-492e-aa5a-2335d2dadc8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData["hm"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e464dc0-e365-4a10-a441-284b95d9de43"],
 " here is an entirely different construction from the split-step \
trajectories, so the reference and the ensemble share nothing but the \
physics. All three agree to within the Monte-Carlo scatter of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox["3000"], "\[TildeTilde]", "1.8", "%"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47987567-64b8-4b66-8a88-dfe1c82cec5b"],
 ", including the purity, which falls from ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d8647710-908d-462a-88e5-e8d86cd9ceaf"],
 " to about ",
 Cell[BoxData["0.65"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "882d90d5-30b6-4347-b262-cbf8029ee8d6"],
 " while every individual trajectory stays exactly pure. That contrast is the \
whole conceptual content of an unravelling, and here you watch both sides of \
it in one cell."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9044661a-a81b-4684-a315-afbadf8956ff"],

Cell["The Failure Mode: Heating Off the Edge of the Grid", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6a21dca5-05a2-4781-965b-b8fe3668585e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every simulation has a regime where it lies, and you want to meet yours \
deliberately. Recall the exact heating law: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d53c", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cf3a314-fefe-4ed8-8406-629a09cb2d28"],
 " grows as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e217e99-7bdd-47dc-a15b-508cd63bc732"],
 " without bound. But a grid of spacing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fe0fe4f-a91e-495f-ba01-c1ecdfc16fc0"],
 " can only represent momenta up to the Nyquist value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["max",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "549de59a-f603-4f65-8a5c-c5e5d137a755"],
 ". Sooner or later the packet heats past what the grid can hold. Watch a \
deliberately coarse grid meet that limit, against a fine one and against the \
exact law:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a778e806-ec1e-4a30-a51f-8e967f7562a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "=", " ", "40."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.0005"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"coarse", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
       RowBox[{"64", ",", " ", "40."}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"fine", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
       RowBox[{"512", ",", " ", "40."}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"0.25", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}], " ", "tt"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"p2Exp", "[", 
             RowBox[{"coarse", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"stepSym", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"coarse", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"0.", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"coarse", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
                   "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "tt", ",", 
                 " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", "\n", "         ", 
               RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                "coarse", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], 
                "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "40", "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"p2Exp", "[", 
             RowBox[{"fine", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"stepSym", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"fine", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"0.", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"fine", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
                   "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "tt", ",", 
                 " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", "\n", "         ", 
               RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                "fine", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], 
                "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "40", "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0.25", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "1.0"}], "}"}]}], 
        "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<exact law\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<N=64 (p_max^2=25)\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<N=512\>\""}], 
         "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[38]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7338daef-058a-477a-871a-7a2edb4d61b6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The coarse grid does not diverge, does not warn, and does not stop. It \
saturates around ",
 Cell[BoxData["8"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "195cdbf1-480d-43da-a457-e362b9a310c9"],
 " and reports a stable, plausible, completely wrong number, while the fine \
grid tracks the linear growth up to Monte-Carlo scatter. Note that the \
saturation sits below the Nyquist ceiling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["max",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "=", "25"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2e15875-4905-4df5-9631-86793176b052"],
 ", because aliasing folds probability back to low momenta rather than piling \
it up at the edge. This is the failure mode I find genuinely dangerous, \
because the wrong answer looks ",
 StyleBox["more", "TI"],
 " stable than the right one. Refining the time step would never reveal it. \
Only the analytic law does. The practical rule that falls out: your grid must \
resolve ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "87fe7639-d6d4-4a02-9d23-c783f222d002"],
 " from below and accommodate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48e0dee8-751b-4e85-bf7a-4779702cee27"],
 " from above, and those two requirements pull apart as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09bde732-d3ba-44d2-b51d-a1f876a6a6bd"],
 " grows."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f776b4d6-664f-40c9-8205-5eb524b518a2"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us (and What Comes Next)", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"df1c3e1b-22ec-43fe-b75e-2a28a652eb77"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "You now have a complete, computation-first toolkit for continuous \
measurement: a Gaussian detector built from its Kraus operator and validated \
by sampling, the built-in noncommutative algebra yielding the exact heating \
law and the deterministic Riccati system for the conditional variances, a \
closed-form minimum-uncertainty steady state to aim at, the built-in ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "788fafe1-a74f-488c-844b-12f63b2211a5"],
 " stack for an honest general-purpose trajectory simulation, a second-order \
split-step propagator that exponentiates the measurement channel exactly and \
beats the general integrator on the sharp benchmarks, and a verification \
ladder running from a statistics-free consistency test through a full \
Lindblad cross-check to a deliberate encounter with the scheme's own failure \
mode."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c10c7d49-7687-4f36-aea8-238f17727192"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The natural continuations are all one modification away, and I would \
encourage you to try them before reading anything further. Put a double well \
in ",
 Cell[BoxData["pot"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "93f3c073-f645-4f02-be74-d1a63fbf4044"],
 " and watch a delocalized superposition collapse into one lobe, then check \
that it chooses each lobe with the Born probability. Set the detector \
efficiency below one, which breaks purity and forces you from a wavefunction \
to a stochastic master equation. Replace the sharp ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "92273a90-bd03-46a4-9051-caaf7a253df6"],
 " by a spatially smeared version, which is what Di\[OAcute]si and the \
continuous-spontaneous-localization models do to keep the heating rate \
finite. Or measure two non-commuting observables at once and watch the \
conditional state stop being Gaussian."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9c605020-2d25-476a-854a-aa70e6829ffd"],

Cell["\<\
The equation is short, and almost everything interesting about it is a \
consequence of one structural fact: the measurement is diagonal in position. \
Find the analogous fact in your problem, and the integrator will usually \
write itself.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c3bb491a-c400-43dd-85f1-f155bf32316c"]
},
